{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c8ba7f24-738d-4e42-a135-44aa9d8b836b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8258e27dcc2ca01b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-e5wjfeio/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view with multi-select and diff in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the core experiment-comparison capability in the Dashboard:\nusers can select two or more training and pipeline runs from the runs list and\nview their parameters and metrics side by side, plus a diff mode that\nhighlights what changed between two selected runs. Today, parameters and\nmetrics live only on per-run pages, forcing comparison into exported\nspreadsheets; this epic brings that comparison in-platform.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs (training and pipeline runs) from the\n  Dashboard runs list.\n- A comparison view that renders the selected runs' parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- A diff mode within the comparison view that, for two selected runs,\n  highlights which parameters and metrics changed between them.\n- Retrieval of the selected runs' parameters and metrics from the existing\n  run data surfaced by Data Science Pipelines (passive component — no DSP\n  code changes are in scope; see acceptance criteria).\n\nOut of scope (per strategy): automatic best-run selection or promotion, and\ncomparison across clusters or across projects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the Dashboard runs list, when the user selects two or more runs, then\n  a comparison view opens showing each selected run's parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- Given the comparison view with two runs selected, when the user switches to\n  the diff view, then the parameters and metrics that differ between the two\n  runs are highlighted, and unchanged ones are distinguishable from changed\n  ones.\n- Given runs whose parameters and metrics are stored via Data Science\n  Pipelines, when they are selected for comparison, then their parameters and\n  metrics render correctly using the existing DSP run data interfaces\n  (validation that DSP keeps working unmodified as the data source).\n- The comparison view is reachable from the runs list for both training and\n  pipeline runs.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): select two or more runs and view parameters and metrics side by\n  side in the Dashboard — fully covered by this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P1): run diff view highlighting changed parameters and metrics\n  between two selected runs — covered as the diff mode of the comparison view\n  (bundled because it shares the comparison view's UI surface and run data\n  with the P0 work; splitting would build the same surface twice).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28192,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9838049e6f087304","agent_id":"acb7c97fff167479d","session_id":"c3fb0098-5383-4e64-92ab-0a85f474b883","uuid":"af29493a-ecd7-484c-9e26-29c831bf152c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:36:18.003Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
