{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a29c6d7ebd7e6b7b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major.\n13\t\n14\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy\n15\tspans multiple components and teams (Dashboard, Model Registry, Data Science\n16\tPipelines), and HLR-4 calls for substantive documentation authoring — a\n17\tdistinct work stream — so the below-threshold escape conditions do not apply.\n18\t\n19\t## Step 1 — Strategy structure\n20\t\n21\tThe strategy is minimal. Present: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements\n22\t(HLR-1..HLR-4 with priorities), Affected Components (bare list), Out of Scope,\n23\tOpen Questions (none). Missing sections (health warnings, decomposition\n24\tproceeded with available information):\n25\t\n26\t- Affected Components has no per-component change description or owner team.\n27\t- No Impacted Teams table — owner teams were taken from architecture context\n28\t  (`Owning team` per component file).\n29\t- No Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then) section, no\n30\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria below were derived\n31\t  from the HLR wording.\n32\t\n33\tNo Staff Engineer Input section is present.\n34\t\n35\t## Step 2 — Component graph\n36\t\n37\t| Component (canonical) | Role in decomposition | Owner team (from arch context) | Basis |\n38\t|---|---|---|---|\n39\t| Dashboard | Active — comparison UI (runs list + registry entry point) | RHOAI Dashboard | HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 |\n40\t| Model Registry | Active — run lineage on registered model versions | Model Registry | HLR-2 |\n41\t| Data Science Pipelines | Passive — existing source of run parameters/metrics; no change described | RHOAI Pipelines | see note below |\n42\t\n43\tAll three components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (rhoai-3.0) and\n44\tare Konflux-onboarded — no onboarding chain (Rule 20) and no license-validation\n45\tepic is needed. No component is new.\n46\t\n47\t**Passive component note (Data Science Pipelines):** the strategy lists DSP as\n48\taffected but describes no change to it, and architecture context confirms\n49\tpipeline runs (with their parameters and metrics) are already surfaced in the\n50\tDashboard through the existing DSP interfaces. Per Step 2, DSP is treated as a\n51\tpassive component: validation that the comparison view renders real run\n52\tparameters and metrics becomes an acceptance criterion on the Dashboard\n53\tcomparison epic. If implementation reveals that comparing multiple runs\n54\trequires a DSP-side change (e.g. bulk retrieval), that is an implementation\n55\tdetail for the Dashboard team to resolve or escalate — it is not a genuine\n56\tunknown that changes which epics exist (the strategy's Open Questions section\n57\tis empty).\n58\t\n59\tNo non-obvious component-name mappings were needed; all affected components\n60\tmatch canonical names in `.context/rhai-components.txt` exactly. The\n61\tdocumentation epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component.\n62\t\n63\t## Step 3 — Investigations\n64\t\n65\tThe strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and contains no risks table,\n66\tassumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. A full scan found no\n67\tgenuine unknowns whose resolution would change which epics exist or what they\n68\tdo. No Investigation epics.\n69\t\n70\t## Epic List\n71\t\n72\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n73\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view with multi-select and diff in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Record originating run linkage on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P1 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open a run comparison from the Model Registry UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n77\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n78\t\n79\tEpic count: 4 (main plan, no branch epics).\n80\t\n81\t## Dependency DAG\n82\t\n83\t```mermaid\n84\tgraph TD\n85\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9015-E001<br/>Dashboard comparison view + diff]\n86\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9015-E002<br/>Model Registry run lineage]\n87\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9015-E003<br/>Registry comparison entry point]\n88\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-9015-E004<br/>Comparison workflow docs]\n89\t    E001 --> E003\n90\t    E002 --> E003\n91\t    E001 --> E004\n92\t    E002 --> E004\n93\t    E003 --> E004\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\tCritical path: E001 → E003 → E004 (3 epics).\n97\t\n98\t## DAG Justification\n99\t\n100\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n101\t|------|------|-----------|\n102\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different repos (odh-dashboard vs model-registry), no shared artifacts — parallel |\n103\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 | The registry entry point opens the comparison view that the Dashboard comparison epic produces; it builds against that UI surface and its selected-runs handling |\n104\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 | The registry entry point consumes the run-linkage data that the Model Registry epic records on model versions; the consuming implementation is serial after the producing one |\n105\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics (docs describe what was built) |\n106\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same |\n107\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same |\n108\t\n109\tNo Investigation epics exist, so no gated_by / gate_failure_impact fields and\n110\tno conditional branches apply.\n111\t\n112\t## HLR