{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a25b2492ffa2cf81","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tscore: 11\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: major\n8\t  criterion: HLR Coverage\n9\t  description: 'E001 bundles HLR-3 (P1 run diff view) into the P0 comparison-view\n10\t    epic — priority collapse with a distinct deferrable feature. The stated justification\n11\t    (splitting would build the same surface twice) is incorrect: a diff-mode epic\n12\t    would depend on and extend the comparison view, not rebuild it. Split HLR-3 into\n13\t    a separate P1 epic depending on the P0 epic.'\n14\t- severity: minor\n15\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n16\t  description: 'human_process_gates is scored inconsistently across sibling implementation\n17\t    epics: E002=1 and E003=0 on identical no-approval-steps rationales, and E001=0\n18\t    on a hedged rationale. Per the rubric, None maps to +1; score the three implementation\n19\t    epics consistently.'\n20\terror: null\n21\t---\n22\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9015\n23\t\n24\t## Review Summary\n25\t\n26\tScore: 11/14 — fail\n27\tRecommendation: revise\n28\t\n29\tAuto-fail rule triggered: Criterion 1 (HLR Coverage) scores 0 due to a major\n30\tpriority-collapse issue, so the decomposition fails regardless of total score.\n31\t\n32\t## Criterion Details\n33\t\n34\t### 1. HLR Coverage (0/2)\n35\t\n36\t**Major — priority collapse in E001 (HLR-1 P0 + HLR-3 P1).** E001 bundles\n37\tHLR-3 (P1, run diff view) into the P0 side-by-side comparison epic. HLR-3 is a\n38\tdistinct deferrable feature, not incidental polish on the P0 work: the strategy\n39\tenumerates it as its own HLR with its own priority, it is a separately\n40\tuser-visible capability (a diff mode highlighting changed parameters/metrics\n41\tbetween two runs) with its own acceptance criteria, and the P0 side-by-side\n42\tcomparison delivers value without it — which is exactly what the strategy's\n43\tP0/P1 split signals. The bundling justification (\"splitting would force two\n44\tepics to build the same surface independently\") is incorrect: a diff-mode epic\n45\twould depend on the comparison-view epic and extend its existing surface (Rule\n46\t13 consuming edge), not rebuild it. The effect of the bundling is that the P0\n47\tcapability cannot be planned, shipped, or deferred independently of a P1\n48\tfeature — the planning requirement that overrides boundary convenience. HLR-3\n49\tshould be a separate P1 epic depending on the P0 comparison-view epic.\n50\t\n51\tOtherwise coverage is complete: all four HLRs map to epics, the traceability\n52\tmatrix is present and accurate, priority inheritance is correct (E003 P1\n53\tenables no P0 work; E004 is docs-authoring and exempt, its P1 correctly derived\n54\tfrom the strategy's Major priority), and this is a full decomposition (triage\n55\tabsent), so multi-epic output is expected.\n56\t\n57\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n58\t\n59\tNo circular dependencies. Diagram edges exactly match epic frontmatter\n60\tdependencies in both directions (E001 deps [], E002 deps [], E003 deps\n61\t[E001,E002], E004 deps [E001,E002,E003]), and arrows run dependency → dependent\n62\tper convention. Edges are justified: E001→E003 (consumes the comparison-view\n63\tUI surface) and E002→E003 (consumes the run-linkage data via the REST API) are\n64\tgenuine data/artifact dependencies under Rule 13; the E001/E002→E004 edges are\n65\tRule 11 docs-authoring edges (valid, not flagged as serialization). E001 ∥ E002\n66\tparallelism is correctly preserved (different repos, no shared artifacts). No\n67\tkonflux-onboarding or license-validation epics exist — verified against\n68\tarchitecture context, all three components are Konflux-onboarded, so no Rule 20\n69\tchain or parallelism rules 7/8/10 apply. Critical path length 3 is appropriate\n70\tfor a strategy of this size. No uncaptured data dependencies found in epic\n71\tcontent; no branch files exist.\n72\t\n73\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n74\t\n75\tComponent/team tuples are cleanly separated: E001/E003 (Dashboard / RHOAI\n76\tDashboard), E002 (Model Registry / Model Registry), E004 (Documentation / RHOAI\n77\tDocumentation). Teams match architecture context owning-team values. No scope\n78\tduplication across siblings — E001 builds the comparison view, E002 records\n79\tlinkage data, E003 composes both as an entry point, E004 documents. No\n80\twork-product type mixing (code epics are separate from the docs-authoring\n81\tepic). Each epic is well within a single sprint of work.\n82\t\n83\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n84\t\n85\tAll four epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (UI\n86\tview, registry data model + API exposure, UI entry point, documentation\n87\ttopics). No Investigation epics — correctly so: the strategy declares \"Open\n88\tQuestions: None\", and the one candidate unknown (whether comparing runs needs a\n89\tDSP-side change) is correctly handled as a passive-component acceptance\n90\tcriterion rather than a gate, since its answer would not change which epics\n91\texist. No gated_by/gate_failure_impact fields are set, and none are needed.\n92\tE004's implementation_type docs-authoring is correctly applied.\n93\t\n94\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n95\t\n96\tAll epics are Implementation and correctly carry `ai_signals` (not\n97\tinvestigation_signals); all four ai-signals rationale files exist. Most values\n98\tare consistent with the rubric and substantiated by architecture context\n99\t(custom-properties extension point, registry-UI-in-Dashboard, public repos).\n100\t\n101\t**Minor — inconsistent `human_process_gates` across sibling epics.** E002\n102\tscores 1 with rationale \"No approval steps stated; schema/API additions go\n103\tthrough ordinary review\", while E003 scores 0 with the rationale \"No approval\n104\tsteps stated in the strategy\" — identical condition, different values. E001\n105\talso scores 0 on a hedged rationale (\"UI/UX review is possible but not\n106\tmandated\"). Per the rubric, \"None\" maps to +1, so E001/E003's 0 is arguably\n107\tunder-scored; at minimum the three Dashboard/Registry implementation epics\n108\tshould be scored consistently. E004's values are well justified\n109\t(human_process_gates -1 for mandatory docs technical review; repo_access 0 for\n110\tunconfirmed docs toolchain).\n111\t\n112\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n113\t\n114\tEvery epic has testable Given/When/Then-style acceptance criteria derived from\n115\tthe HLR wording. The rule-mandated docs technical-review AC is present on E004.\n116\tThe passive-DSP validation is correctly expressed as an AC on E001 (renders\n117\treal run parameters/metrics via existing DSP interfaces). E003 includes\n118\tgraceful degradation for versions without a recorded run link. No\n119\treplacement/feature-flag or konflux-chain ACs are required (no such epics). No\n120\tepic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n121\t\n122\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n123\t\n124\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: both comparison entry points (runs list in\n125\tE001, registry in E003), the diff view (E001), run linkage recording and\n126\tretrieval (E002), and documentation of the full workflow (E004). Out-of-scope\n127\titems (auto best-run selection, cross-cluster/project comparison) are\n128\tcorrectly excluded and restated in E001. The strategy's minimal sections (no\n129\trisks, no open questions) are handled rather than silently dropped — missing\n130\tsections are called out as health warnings, the DSP passive-component decision\n131\tis documented and converted into an AC, and the docs-team assumption is\n132\tflagged for verification before scheduling.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b19a76517f11dec9","agent_id":"aa48da2d3651432ab","session_id":"c3fb0098-5383-4e64-92ab-0a85f474b883","uuid":"acaa