{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab72ee37dddce951","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Record originating run linkage on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Record originating run linkage on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: a registered model\n34\tversion records a link back to the run that produced it, so that downstream\n35\tconsumers (such as the Dashboard's registry UI) can resolve the originating\n36\trun and open a comparison of candidate runs. Model promotion decisions need\n37\tthis connection between registered versions and the experiments that produced\n38\tthem.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Record, on a registered model version, a reference to the run that produced\n43\t  it, using the Model Registry's existing model-version metadata extension\n44\t  point (custom properties) or an equivalent registry-native mechanism — the\n45\t  concrete representation is an implementation decision for the Model Registry\n46\t  team.\n47\t- Make the recorded run linkage retrievable through the Model Registry REST\n48\t  API so clients can resolve the originating run for any registered model\n49\t  version.\n50\t- Registration flows (or registrating users/tools) are able to supply the\n51\t  originating run reference when a version is registered.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a model version produced by a run, when the version is registered,\n56\t  then the registered version carries a link back to that run.\n57\t- Given a registered model version with a recorded run link, when a client\n58\t  queries the Model Registry REST API, then the run linkage is returned and\n59\t  the originating run can be resolved.\n60\t- The linkage mechanism is documented in the Model Registry API surface (e.g.\n61\t  OpenAPI spec) so consumers can build against it.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-2 (P1, data side): registered model versions link back to the run that\n66\t  produced them — the linkage recording and API retrieval half of this HLR is\n67\t  covered by this epic; the registry-UI entry point that consumes it is\n68\t  covered by the Dashboard-side work.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b19a76517f11dec9","agent_id":"aa48da2d3651432ab","session_id":"c3fb0098-5383-4e64-92ab-0a85f474b883","uuid":"dda926a2-82b2-4d5b-b002-57471ca875fc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:44:39.849Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab72ee37dddce951","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
