{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b0148bae1d49813","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major.\n13\t\n14\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy\n15\tspans multiple components and teams (Dashboard, Model Registry, Data Science\n16\tPipelines), and HLR-4 calls for substantive documentation authoring — a\n17\tdistinct work stream — so the below-threshold escape conditions do not apply.\n18\t\n19\t## Step 1 — Strategy structure\n20\t\n21\tThe strategy is minimal. Present: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements\n22\t(HLR-1..HLR-4 with priorities), Affected Components (bare list), Out of Scope,\n23\tOpen Questions (none). Missing sections (health warnings, decomposition\n24\tproceeded with available information):\n25\t\n26\t- Affected Components has no per-component change description or owner team.\n27\t- No Impacted Teams table — owner teams were taken from architecture context\n28\t  (`Owning team` per component file).\n29\t- No Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then) section, no\n30\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria below were derived\n31\t  from the HLR wording.\n32\t\n33\tNo Staff Engineer Input section is present.\n34\t\n35\t## Step 2 — Component graph\n36\t\n37\t| Component (canonical) | Role in decomposition | Owner team (from arch context) | Basis |\n38\t|---|---|---|---|\n39\t| Dashboard | Active — comparison UI (runs list + registry entry point) | RHOAI Dashboard | HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 |\n40\t| Model Registry | Active — run lineage on registered model versions | Model Registry | HLR-2 |\n41\t| Data Science Pipelines | Passive — existing source of run parameters/metrics; no change described | RHOAI Pipelines | see note below |\n42\t\n43\tAll three components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (rhoai-3.0) and\n44\tare Konflux-onboarded — no onboarding chain (Rule 20) and no license-validation\n45\tepic is needed. No component is new.\n46\t\n47\t**Passive component note (Data Science Pipelines):** the strategy lists DSP as\n48\taffected but describes no change to it, and architecture context confirms\n49\tpipeline runs (with their parameters and metrics) are already surfaced in the\n50\tDashboard through the existing DSP interfaces. Per Step 2, DSP is treated as a\n51\tpassive component: validation that the comparison view renders real run\n52\tparameters and metrics becomes an acceptance criterion on the Dashboard\n53\tcomparison epic. If implementation reveals that comparing multiple runs\n54\trequires a DSP-side change (e.g. bulk retrieval), that is an implementation\n55\tdetail for the Dashboard team to resolve or escalate — it is not a genuine\n56\tunknown that changes which epics exist (the strategy's Open Questions section\n57\tis empty).\n58\t\n59\tNo non-obvious component-name mappings were needed; all affected components\n60\tmatch canonical names in `.context/rhai-components.txt` exactly. The\n61\tdocumentation epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component.\n62\t\n63\t## Step 3 — Investigations\n64\t\n65\tThe strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and contains no risks table,\n66\tassumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. A full scan found no\n67\tgenuine unknowns whose resolution would change which epics exist or what they\n68\tdo. No Investigation epics.\n69\t\n70\t## Epic List\n71\t\n72\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n73\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view with multi-select in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Record originating run linkage on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P1 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open a run comparison from the Model Registry UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n77\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n78\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E005 | Run diff view between two selected runs | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n79\t\n80\tEpic count: 5 (main plan, no branch epics).\n81\t\n82\t## Dependency DAG\n83\t\n84\t```mermaid\n85\tgraph TD\n86\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9015-E001<br/>Dashboard comparison view]\n87\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9015-E002<br/>Model Registry run lineage]\n88\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9015-E003<br/>Registry comparison entry point]\n89\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-9015-E004<br/>Comparison workflow docs]\n90\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-9015-E005<br/>Run diff view]\n91\t    E001 --> E003\n92\t    E002 --> E003\n93\t    E001 --> E005\n94\t    E001 --> E004\n95\t    E002 --> E004\n96\t    E003 --> E004\n97\t    E005 --> E004\n98\t```\n99\t\n100\tCritical path: E001 → E003 → E004 and E001 → E005 → E004 (3 epics).\n101\t\n102\t## DAG Justification\n103\t\n104\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n105\t|------|------|-----------|\n106\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different repos (odh-dashboard vs model-registry), no shared artifacts — parallel |\n107\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 | The registry entry point opens the comparison view that the Dashboard comparison epic produces; it builds against that UI surface and its selected-runs handling |\n108\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 | The registry entry point consumes the run-linkage data that the Model Registry epic records on model versions; the consuming implementation is serial after the producing one |\n109\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 13 | The diff view consumes the comparison view's UI surface and selected-runs handling; it extends that existing surface (consuming edge), it does not rebuild it |\n110\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics (docs describe what was built) |\n111\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same |\n112\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same |\n113\t| E005 → E004 | Rule 11 | Same — the docs cover the diff view |\n114\t\n115\tNo Investigation epics exist, so no gated_by / gate_failure_impact fields and\n116\tno conditional branches apply.\n117\t\n118\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n119\t\n120\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) |\n121\t|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|\n122\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Select two or more runs, view parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 |\n123\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Registered model versions link back to the producing run; comparison openable from the Model Registry | RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 (linkage data), RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 (registry entry point) |\n124\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Run diff view highlighting changed parameters and metrics between two runs | RHAISTRAT-9015-E005 |\n125\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers the comparison workflow from runs list and registry | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 |\n126\t\n127\tFull coverage — no orphaned HLRs.\n128\t\n129\t**Split decision (HLR-1 in the comparison-view epic, HLR-3 in the diff-view\n130\tepic):** HLR-3 (P1, run diff view) is a distinct, deferrable feature — the\n131\tstrategy enumerates it as its own HLR with its own priority and its own\n132\tacceptance criteria, and the P0 side-by-side comparison delivers value without\n133\tit. The diff-view epic depends on and extends the comparison view's existing\n134\tsurface (Rule 13 consuming edge) rather than rebuilding it, so the split does\n135\tnot duplicate work. The comparison-view epic keeps HLR-1's P0; the diff-view\n136\tepic inherits HLR-3's P1.\n137\t\n138\t**Priority notes:**\n139\t- E003 inherits HLR-2's P1.\n140\t- E005 inherits HLR-3's P1.\n141\t- E004 is a docs-authoring epic: exempt from priority inheritance; its P1 is\n142\t  derived from the strategy frontmatter priority (Major → P1), not from\n143\t  HLR-4's P2. See health warnings.\n144\t\n145\t## Health Warnings (non-blocking)\n146\t\n147\t1. **Missing strategy sections** — no Impacted Teams table, no per-component\n148\t   change descriptions, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance\n149\t   criteria, no NFRs. Teams were sourced from architecture context; the\n150\t   documentation epic's owning team (\"RHOAI Documentation\") is an assumption\n151\t   because no docs owner is named anywhere in the strategy — verify before\n152\t   scheduling.\n153\t2. **Data Science Pipelines listed as affected with no described change** —\n154\t   treated as a passive data source (see Step 2 note). If comparing multiple\n155\t   runs turns out to require DSP API changes, that work is currently\n156\t   unrepresented and would need a follow-up epic.\n157\t3. **Docs priority above its HLR** — HLR-4 is P2 but the docs-authoring epic\n158\t   is P1 per the docs priority exception (strategy priority Major). Not a\n159\t   priority inversion in the ordinary sense, but reviewers should be aware\n160\t   the docs epic will sort above HLR-4's stated priority.\n161\t4. **Requirement overlap** — the problem statement notes requirements were\n162\t   consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept;\n163\t   HLR-1/HLR-3 overlap in particular was resolved by splitting into separate\n164\t   epics (the P0 comparison view and the P1 diff view), with the diff-view\n165\t   epic depending on the comparison view.\n166\t\n167\t## Tiered Delivery\n168\t\n169\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing. All work is\n170\tin-platform across components that are GA and onboarded.\n171\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9708d20ca5a7675","agent_id":"af9b9aa4f201571a5","session_id":"c3fb0098-5383-4e64-92ab-0a85f474b883","uuid":"44b3ab90-66a0-4546